  "worked_solution": "To map the entire region $\u0394$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the side ${S}_{4}.$\n\nFor the side ${S}_{4},$ we have $u=0$ and $1\\ge v\\ge 0.$ Substituting $u=0$ into our transformation equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =((u-1)v,\\,uv-1) \\\\  & =((0-1)v,\\,(0)v-1) \\\\  & =(-v,-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the image of ${S}_{4}$ can be parametrized by\n\n$$\nx=-v,\\,y=-1,\\,1\\ge v\\ge 0.\n$$\n\n \n\nWriting this in the usual notation, we have\n\n$$\nx(t)=-t,\\,y(t)=-1,\\,1\\ge t\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nThis is a horizontal line segment with endpoints $(-1,-1)$ and $(0,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14046771/assets/48ae89e14005e5fc21f0693e769e6214c1c9a94ba0cd63e7ce08d9771fbf82f1.png)",
